{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788484210-3cFKaOBZBzdAyjhyZM4n","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything passes. Let me summarize the work.\n\nSummary of the change (matching upstream PR #1198, \"Realtime: make sure we use the initial model settings\"):\n\n**Root cause:** `RealtimeSession._get_updated_model_settings_from_agent` built settings from an empty dict, filled in agent-derived instructions/tools/handoffs, then did `updated_settings.update(initial_settings)` — so:\n- `run_config[\"model_settings\"]` (settings passed to `RealtimeRunner.__init__`) was completely ignored.\n- `model_config[\"initial_model_settings\"]` (passed to `run()`) clobbered agent-derived settings — including on handoffs, where the new agent's instructions/tools/handoffs were overwritten by the original run's initial settings.\n\n**Fix:** merge order is now run_config → model config initial settings → agent-derived settings (with tracing-disabled applied last).\n\nI should present this concisely with file:line references.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b990b0-ca4b-481f-a781-dd48cfe3ddbd","uuid":"8da32845-1f1e-463c-97a1-cadfc30a6c82","timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:10:20.053Z","request_id":"gen-1788484210-3cFKaOBZBzdAyjhyZM4n"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788484210-3cFKaOBZBzdAyjhyZM4n","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The fix is in place and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `RealtimeSession._get_updated_model_settings_from_agent`, settings were built from an empty dict, filled with agent-derived `instructions`/`tools`/`handoffs`, and then the model config's `initial_model_settings` were applied **on top** via `update()`. Two consequences:\n\n- `run_config[\"model_settings\"]` — the settings you pass to `RealtimeRunner.__init__()` — was **never read at all**.\n- `initial_model_settings` from `run()` clobbered agent-derived settings, so on a handoff the new agent's instructions/tools/handoffs were overwritten by the initial run's values instead of being merged.\n\n## The fix — `src/agents/realtime/session.py`\n\nMerge order is now: **run config → initial model settings → agent-derived settings**, with `tracing_disabled` still applied last:\n\n- `_get_updated_model_settings_from_agent` (`session.py:511`) now takes a `starting_settings` parameter, seeds the result with a copy of `run_config[\"model_settings\"]`, layers `starting_settings` over it, then applies agent-derived `instructions`/`tools`/`handoffs` — so agent-specific values augment the base configuration rather than the base wiping them out.\n- Initial connection (`session.py:123`) passes `starting_settings=self._model_config.get(\"initial_model_settings\", None)` — your initialization-time model config is respected as the foundation.\n- Handoff handling (`session.py:332`) passes `starting_settings=None` — the incoming agent's settings are computed from the run-config base plus that agent's own values, so a stale agent's settings don't leak across the transition.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Updated `tests/realtime/test_session.py`: the old test asserted initial settings override agent instructions (the buggy behavior); it now asserts agent-derived settings win while model-config settings like `voice`/`model_name` are preserved. Added `TestModelSettingsPrecedence` covering all three cases: both configs, run-config-only fallback, and model-config-only.\n- Updated `tests/realtime/test_tracing.py` for the new method signature.\n\n**Verification:** all 103 realtime tests pass; `ruff format`, `ruff check`, and `mypy` are clean. The full suite shows the same 13 pre-existing failures (`test_reasoning_content.py`, missing optional `litellm`/voice deps) both before and after the change — unrelated to this fix.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9b990b0-ca4b-481f-a781-dd48cfe3ddbd","uuid":"be783267-70ef-4fd0-ba58-2aebd6ffaaca","timestamp":"2026-09-04T01:10:31.486Z","request_id":"gen-1788484210-3cFKaOBZBzdAyjhyZM4n"}
