itten by the initial run's values instead of being merged.\n\n## The fix — `src/agents/realtime/session.py`\n\nMerge order is now: **run config → initial model settings → agent-derived settings**, with `tracing_disabled` still applied last:\n\n- `_get_updated_model_settings_from_agent` (`session.py:511`) now takes a `starting_settings` parameter, seeds the result with a copy of `run_config[\"model_settings\"]`, layers `starting_settings` over it, then applies agent-derived `instructions`/`tools`/`handoffs` — so agent-specific values augment the base configuration rather than the base wiping them out.\n- Initial connection (`session.py:123`) passes `starting_settings=self._model_config.get(\"initial_model_settings\", None)` — your initialization-time model config is respected as the foundation.\n- Handoff handling (`session.py:332`) passes `starting_settings=None` — the incoming agent's settings are computed from the run-config base plus that agent's own values, so a stale agent's settings don't leak across the transition.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Updated `tests/realtime/test_session.py`: the old test asserted initial settings override agent instructions (the buggy behavior); it now asserts agent-derived settings win while model-config settings like `voice`/`model_name` are preserved. Added `TestModelSettingsPrecedence` covering all three cases: both configs, run-config-only fallback, and model-config-only.\n- Updated `tests/realtime/test_tracing.py` for the new method signature.\n\n**Verification:** all 103 realtime tests pass; `ruff format`, `ruff check`, and `mypy` are clean. The full suite shows the same 13 pre-existing failures (`test_reasoning_content.py`, missing optional `litellm`/voice deps) both before and after the change — unrelated to this fix.","ttft_ms":2615,"type":"result","duration_ms":377866,"uuid":"d305f225-5eb4-4ae0-aa56-c1001171f339","ttft_stream_ms":2604,"time_to_request_ms":98,"first_content_frame_ms":2605,"queued_turn_count":0}

